/// New York City resident income tax.
///
/// Everyone who `lives us/ny/nyc` pays city income tax on top of New York State
/// and federal tax, so this is the third link of the chain `us`, `us/ny`,
/// `us/ny/nyc`. The city taxes the same base as the state: federal adjusted
/// gross income, less the New York standard deduction (declared by `us/ny`,
/// which this system includes). Tax withheld or paid to the city during the
/// year is credited.
///
/// Simplified on purpose: it leaves out credits and the city's part-year
/// resident rules. Only the `single` and `joint` filing statuses have figures.
///
/// SAMPLE DATA. The figures are community-maintained and were written from the
/// published tables, not checked against the Department of Taxation and
/// Finance. Verify them against the NY DTF (tax.ny.gov, "New York City
/// resident tax rates") before relying on them, and correct them in a pull
/// request when they are wrong.
system us/ny/nyc

use us/ny


/// The New York City Department of Finance.
entity nyc-dof : government

/// New York City income tax withheld from pay, or paid to the city directly.
/// Every arrival counts as city tax already paid.
kind nyc-tax : expense


/// Tax withheld from pay, or paid in installments, is credited against the
/// city tax owed for the year. Send money to a place of kind `nyc-tax`, or let
/// a paycheck leg do it.
law credit-nyc-withholding
  on in
  when to is nyc-tax
  count amount as nyc-withheld

/// New York City resident income tax for the year (Administrative Code §11-1701),
/// on the same taxable income as the state. Tax already withheld or paid is
/// credited, and the rest is owed by April 15 of the next year (Form IT-201).
/// A refund is not booked.
law city-income-tax
  each year
  let taxable = max(tally(agi) - deduction[year, owner.filing], empty)
  let liability = progressive(brackets[year, owner.filing], taxable)
  count liability as nyc-income-tax
  owe max(liability - tally(nyc-withheld), empty) to nyc-dof by date(year + 1, 4, 15) as nyc-income-tax


// The marginal rate above each threshold. They have not changed in years, so
// the 2024 rows apply to every later year until a new row is written.
// verify: the rows against the DTF's current resident rate schedule.
param brackets
  2024 single      0 USD 3.078% | 12_000 USD 3.762% | 25_000 USD 3.819% | 50_000 USD 3.876%
  2024 joint       0 USD 3.078% | 21_600 USD 3.762% | 45_000 USD 3.819% | 90_000 USD 3.876%
